// title: "High-speed rail piece catalogue"
// summary: "Generate the reusable-type index, canonical picture links, and scoped coverage from authoritative piece and observation records."
//
// Used when: A contributor or catalogue inspection needs a generated snapshot of the registered reusable rail types, picture paths, design flags, route counts, and recorded manual coverage.
// Read by: Human readers and catalogue regression checks; it accompanies 00_pieces/INVENTORY.md as generated data. Normal library builds load each registered piece.json directly, rather than this copied catalogue snapshot.
// Updated by: scp.inventory.write_inventories, called by python3 -B custom-pieces/scp.py inventory and the full documentation refresh, reads current definitions, connection records, image availability, and checks/manual-tests.json. Edit those owning records and regenerate.
// Affects: The browseable piece index and reported coverage. Each piece definition and observation record remains authoritative; a generated count or checkmark does not add an observation, approve an image, or verify a historical record under a renamed ID.
// Reference: custom-pieces/docs/WORKFLOW_DOCUMENTATION_GENERATION.md#9-maintain-the-complete-preview-catalogue.
